      "content": "The color-coded tags sound like a good visual cue. \n\nI'm also thinking about the \"vibe\" of the event. Since it's a law firm, it needs to be very polished and sophisticated, but I don't want the allergy warnings to look like industrial warning signs or cheap plastic cards. It might kill the elegance of the buffet. \n\nDo you have any ideas for how to make these safety labels and communication methods feel high-end and integrated into the decor, rather than just looking like a bunch of warning signs stuck on the table?",
